      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T03:21:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "thanks for the review and the dstailed explanation.the driver is sipa,UNISOC\u0027s network accelerator,running as an out-of-tree GKI vendor module. it can\u0027t be upstreamed in the near term - it depends on undocumented UNISOC soc hardware,and there is no UNISOC bringup in mainline that could exercise it.out rx buffers come from a dedicated cma area,so we register \u0027mp_ops-\u003erelease_netmem\u0027 to return pages to that CMA pool via \u0027cma_release\u0027 instead of the buddy allocator.However,the mp_ops rodata check only accepts vmlinux rodata,which effectively blocks any GKI vendor module from using the memory-provider mechanism. given the driver can\u0027t be upstreamed soon,could you suggest a more reasonable way forward on the kernel side?",
